WARN testdata/warn/shell-and-inherit.yaml:2:14  W1002: the job inherits SSH_AUTH_SOCK, HTTPS_PROXY from the environment paceq was started in

   1 | name: legacy-import
>  2 | inherit_env: [SSH_AUTH_SOCK, HTTPS_PROXY]
                    ^
   3 | steps:

   A job starts from an empty environment on purpose (08 section 3.2): what it gets is
   what the file says, so a run from a terminal and a run from the scheduler are the
   same run. Every name here is an exception, and it makes the job depend on how
   paceq itself was started.

   Set the value in the job instead, when it is not a secret:

       env:
         NAME: value

   paceq error W1002  for the full explanation

WARN testdata/warn/shell-and-inherit.yaml:6:12  W1001: the step "sync" runs its command through a shell

   4 |   - name: sync
   5 |     run: ["rsync -a /srv/a/ /srv/b/"]
>  6 |     shell: true
                  ^

   A shell splits, globs and expands what it is given, so an argument that carries a
   space, a quote or a semicolon stops being one argument. With shell off, paceq
   starts the process itself and nothing touches the arguments:

       run: ["/bin/sh", "-c", "echo done"]

   Keep it on only when the command genuinely needs a shell, and say why in the
   description.

   paceq error W1001  for the full explanation
